QuestGuidance.Register("en",111,{
[3521]="7000B8D2\n1\tPour Gandalf's draught into the burning cauldron\030Bring Gandalf's draught to the burning cauldron\tThe burning cauldron is in a tall wooden structure in Ghâshru to the north-east. Eywind told you to pour Gandalf's draught into the cauldron which the goblins use to produce their fire-pots and tip it over so the mixture will ignite the materials throughout the encampment.\n2\tSpeak with Eywind near the entrance to the High Pass\tTell Eywind of the destruction wrought by Gandalf's draught at the burning cauldron.\n",
[3522]="700413BA\n1\tSpeak with Laerind\tLaerind can be found in the village of Ethring. You should speak with Laerind.\n2\tSpeak with Borhador\tBorhador can be found in the village of Ethring. You should speak with Borhador.\n3\tSeek out Garvir in Linhir\tGarvir, the leader of the Dor-en-Ernil's Gondorian forces can be found in the city of Linhir. You should seek out Garvir in Linhir.\n",
[3523]="70000154\n1\tConfront the Old Took's ghost\tThe ghost's presence is strongest in the far corner of Adelard's library, near the small book-shelf. After all else failed, Adelard Took has asked you to enter his library and confront the ghost of the Old Took.\n2\tTalk to Adelard Took\tAdelard Took is outside the library in the Great Smials. In confronting the \"ghost\" in Adelard Took's library, you discovered that it was nothing more than a squirrel hiding behind the book-case. You should tell Adelard that it is safe to return to his library.\n",
[3524]="70059321\n1\tExamine the situation at the western gate of Trestlebridge (total: 2)\tSomething was placed at the western gate of Trestlebridge. You should examine the situation there.\n2\tTalk to Aran Greenwith\tAran Greenwith can be found at Trestlebridge. You should talk to Aran Greenwith.\n3\tTalk to Aran Greenwith near Cotfast\tAran Greenwith can be found near Cotfast in the Wildwood. You should talk to Aran Greenwith near Cotfast.\n4\tEnter Cotfast\tCotfast can be found in the Wildwood. You should enter Cotfast.\n5\tDestroy Orc bounties (total: 8)\030Collect bribing gold (total: 8)\030Defeat enemies in Cotfast (total: 10)\tOrc bounties and bribing gold can be found in Cotfast. You should destroy the Orc bounties, collect the bribing gold, and defeat foes at Cotfast.\n6\tKnock on the door where Gothtal is holed up\tThe building in which Gothtal is holed up can be found in Cotfast. You should knock on the door and confront Gothtal.\n7\tSound the Cotfast village alarm\030Defeat Gothtal\tThe Cotfast village alarm can be found nearby. You should sound the alarm to get Gothtal's attention.\n8\tTalk to Aran Greenwith near Cotfast\tAran Greenwith can be found near Cotfast in the Wildwood. You should talk to Aran Greenwith near Cotfast.\n9\tTalk to Aran Greenwith at Trestlebridge\tAran Greenwith can be found at Trestlebridge. You should talk to Aran Greenwith.\n10\tReconstruction work continues on Trestlebridge. You should survey the reconstruction of Trestlebridge.\t\n11\tTalk to Aran Greenwith at Trestlebridge\tAran Greenwith can be found at Trestlebridge. You should talk to Aran Greenwith.\n",
[3525]="700660DD\n1\tTalk to Dervorin\tDervorin is going to confront Dravron over his taxes, or lack thereof. Talk to him when you're ready to accompany him.\n2\tTalk to Dervorin\tYou have returned to Ethring with Dervorin. Talk to Dervorin.\n",
[3526]="7005467D\n1\tDrive Shakfut from the area\030Defeat Shakfut's supporters (total: 6)\tShakfut is currently leading Ugrukhôr's troops in this area. He has been able to prevent his forces from pushing towards Gothmog's encampment on the western side of the Circle of Wrath. You should drive off Shakfut and defeat his most loyal warriors.\n2\tTalk to Dolenthol\tYou have driven away Shakfut and his most loyal supporters. You should return to Dolenthol and inform him of your victory.\n",
[3527]="70067F51\n1\tInform Ayaluk that the overseer will be brought to justice\tNûrut directed you to inform Ayaluk that he will confront the overseer and that the brother is expected to stand witness. Find Ayaluk at his family home in Rakhatâb.\n2\tReport the news to Foreman Nûrut\tAyaluk was not within his hovel. You discovered a small pool of fresh blood in his stead. Deliver this news to the guard.\n3\tFind Ulanor and rescue Ayaluk\tUlanor is taking Ayaluk to the Corsairs for some evil purpose. Stop her and save Ayaluk.\n4\tSpeak with Foreman Nûrut at Rakhatâb\tWith the overseer apprehended and Ayaluk safely returned to Rhakatâb you should make your way to the foreman and inform him of the good news.\n",
[3528]="700351D6\n1\tDefeat White Hand enemies in Byre Tor (total: 8)\tThe forces of Isengard can be found throughout Byre Tor in the High Knolls. You should defeat the cruel new masters of Byre Tor.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many foes in Byre Tor to avenge the villagers who lost their homes and their lives.\n",
[3529]="70058AEC\n1\tDefeat the Beasts of Slaughter\tGorgar's trap has been sprung, and you must now fight in his arena or perish. You should defeat Gorgar's Beasts of Slaughter.\n2\tDefeat Gorgar and Ránulur\tYou have defeated the beasts, but Gorgar now intends to fight you himself! You must now face Gorgar the Ruthless and Ránulur, Chieftain of Wargs in the arena!\n3\tCompleted: Conquering the Bloody Threshold (Tier 1)\tYou have completed the Amdân Dammul, the Bloody Threshold on Tier 1.\n",
[3530]="70058AF8\n1\tDefeat the Beasts of Slaughter\tGorgar's trap has been sprung, and you must now fight in his arena or perish. You should defeat Gorgar's Beasts of Slaughter.\n2\tDefeat Gorgar and Ránulur\tYou have defeated the beasts, but Gorgar now intends to fight you himself! You must now face Gorgar the Ruthless and Ránulur, Chieftain of Wargs in the arena!\n3\tCompleted: Conquering the Bloody Threshold (Tier 2)\tYou have completed the Amdân Dammul, the Bloody Threshold on Tier 2.\n",
[3531]="70058AF9\n1\tDefeat the Beasts of Slaughter\tGorgar's trap has been sprung, and you must now fight in his arena or perish. You should defeat Gorgar's Beasts of Slaughter.\n2\tDefeat Gorgar and Ránulur\tYou have defeated the beasts, but Gorgar now intends to fight you himself! You must now face Gorgar the Ruthless and Ránulur, Chieftain of Wargs in the arena!\n3\tCompleted: Conquering the Bloody Threshold (Tier 3)\tYou have completed the Amdân Dammul, the Bloody Threshold on Tier 3.\n",
